    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In Sub-Saharan Africa, the need for hands-on management often stems from a lack of standardized training and adherence to strict protocols, which can be cultural or systemic. Southeast Asia shows a wider spectrum; some areas are highly disciplined, while others require more direct supervision to maintain consistent operational standards. The difference isn't always just skill; it often relates to ingrained work habits and the level of institutional structure present in the local business environment.",
